3.4 Changes and cancellation. This authorization stays in effect until Subcontractor changes or cancels it in writing. A change or cancellation takes effect on the first payment cycle beginning at least three (3) business days after Floor Daddy receives the notice. Subcontractor will notify Floor Daddy immediately if the account is closed or the account details change.
3.5 Authority and accuracy. Subcontractor certifies that it is authorized to direct deposits to and, to the limited extent stated in Section 3.3, debits from the account above, and that the information provided is accurate.
3.6 Compliance. Entries are subject to the NACHA Operating Rules and applicable law. Subcontractor may dispute an unauthorized entry with its financial institution and retains all rights under those rules.

